# Copilot instructions

Read `AGENTS.md` first for stack, commands, layout, and boundaries. This file covers only
Copilot-specific working preferences.

## Working style
- Prefer the smallest change that satisfies the requirement. Do not opportunistically
  refactor surrounding code.
- When a task is ambiguous, propose a plan and stop. Do not guess at product intent.
- Match the surrounding code's existing patterns even where you would choose differently.

## Pull requests you open
- Title: `<type>: <imperative summary>`
- Description states: what changed, why, how it was verified, and what was deliberately
  left out of scope.
- One logical change per PR. If the diff exceeds ~<N> lines, split it.

## Tests
- New behaviour requires a test.
- Tests assert *intended* behaviour. If existing behaviour looks wrong, say so in the PR
  rather than encoding it as the expected result.

## Do not
- Modify the boundaries listed in `AGENTS.md`.
- Add dependencies without saying so explicitly in the PR description.
- Disable, skip, or weaken a failing test to make CI pass.
- Commit generated artifacts, credentials, or `.env` files.

## Handoffs
- Security-sensitive review → `<agent name>`
- Test authoring → `<agent name>`
